\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The positive action of the alternating cycle}
\date{2026-10-25}

\p{Use the [four-cycle](fdip-0003) oriented
#{0\to1\to2\to3\to0}, with edge weights #{(1,t,1,t)}, #{t>0}.
Let #{D:X_V\to X_E} evaluate endpoint differences and #{W} multiply
by the supplied edge weights. With counting adjoint #{D^\dagger}, put
##{L=D^\dagger WD,\qquad Q=L+m^2\operatorname{id},\qquad m>0.}
For every #{x,y}, the [energy interface](fdip-0008) gives
##{h_V(x,Ly)=\sum_e w(e)(Dx)(e)(Dy)(e).}
It is symmetric in #{x,y}, so #{Q} is self-adjoint. On the diagonal
all edge terms are nonnegative and #{m^2h_V(x,x)>0} off zero.
Thus #{Q} is a \vocabk{positive precision parameter}{fdip-0004}.
At zero mass constant fields instead expose the Laplacian kernel.}
\p{In the specified vertex order #{(0,1,2,3)}, write #{x=(a,b,c,d)}.
The four differences are #{b-a,c-b,d-c,a-d}, so the action is exactly
##{\begin{aligned}
2S_{t,m}(a,b,c,d)
 &=(b-a)^2+t(c-b)^2\\
 &\quad +(d-c)^2+t(a-d)^2\\
 &\quad +m^2(a^2+b^2+c^2+d^2).
\end{aligned}}
Each edge occurs once, with one half of its weighted energy in #{S}.
Every summand of #{2S} is nonnegative, with strict positivity off zero
from the mass term.}
\p{Set #{s=1+t+m^2}. The four edge outer products, equivalently
expansion of the four squares, give diagonal coefficient #{s},
cross terms #{-2ab,-2tbc,-2cd,-2tad}, and no #{ac} or #{bd} term.
The [counting array](fdip-002O) is therefore
##{Q_{t,m}=\begin{pmatrix}
s&-1&0&-t\\
-1&s&-t&0\\
0&-t&s&-1\\
-t&0&-1&s
\end{pmatrix}.}
Multiplication recovers #{x^TQ_{t,m}x=2S_{t,m}(x)}.
For #{x=(0,1,0,0)}, the edge energy is #{1+t} and the mass energy
is #{m^2}; hence #{S_{t,m}(0,1,0,0)=s/2}, explicitly #{3/2} when
#{t=m=1}. No change of basis or reference measure occurs.}
\p{This is a direct calculation in the supplied cycle data, with the
edge-once convention of
\citet{Section 2.1, pp. 4-5}{spielman2009effective} and the positive
kinetic sign and half-action of
\citet{Section 4, Equation (4.5), p. 3}{wingate2025lattice}.
All coefficients here are dimensionless. No Gaussian normalizer or
covariance is inferred from the energy calculation.}
